🔴 LEGAL REQUIREMENTS AUDIT (7-POINT GATE)
Agent must verify all 7 with 100% accuracy using live sources. Findings are definitive for Legal review.
Requirement 1: Customer-Facing Feature + Customer Data Processing?
✅ PASS: Model processes customer data (with explicit consent) AND is customer-facing (user approval)
❌ FAIL: Either condition false: (a) no customer consent OR (b) not customer-facing
Verification: Ticket scope, use case description, data flow diagram, consent documentation
Requirement 2: Pre-Approved Open-Source Licenses?
✅ PASS: License on OSS License Classification
⏳ CONDITIONAL: License verified as permissive; Legal confirms pre-approval
❌ FAIL: Restrictive/copyleft license → Legal review required
Verification: Fetch license from model docs; cross-check against wiki
Requirement 3: Pre-Approved Terms of Service (ToS)?
✅ PASS: BOTH cloud platform ToS (AWS/Azure/GCP) AND model vendor ToS (OpenAI/Anthropic/etc.) reviewed + compliant
⏳ CONDITIONAL: New platform or vendor ToS → Legal confirms acceptable
❌ FAIL: Platform or vendor ToS restricts AI use or model deployment
Verification: Confirm current version of (1) cloud platform SLA + ToS, (2) model vendor ToS
Requirement 4: Pre-Approved Acceptable Use Policy (AUP)?
✅ PASS: Use case (internal engineering, security, etc.) complies with BOTH cloud platform AUP AND model vendor AUP
⏳ CONDITIONAL: New vendor AUP or use case undefined → Legal confirms compatible
❌ FAIL: Cloud platform or vendor AUP prohibits intended use (e.g., illegal activity, abuse, content generation)
Verification: Review (1) cloud platform AUP, (2) model vendor AUP; confirm use case does NOT involve prohibited uses
Requirement 5: Sensitive PII Scope Documented?
✅ PASS: All PII types identified + documented (names, email, phone, financial, health, biometric, govt ID); retention policy defined
⏳ CONDITIONAL: PII types unclear → DTS confirms scope documented + retention policy defined
❌ FAIL: ANY PII processed (including anonymized/pseudonymized) without documented scope or retention policy
Verification: Clarify data types (customer names, email, phone, financial data, health/biometric, govt ID); confirm retention policy + audit trail
Requirement 6: Production Models (Not Beta/Preview)?
✅ PASS: All 6 models confirmed production (live in catalogs, not beta/preview)
❌ FAIL: Model marked beta/preview → Legal review required
Verification: Confirm model live in AWS/Azure/Vertex; no beta/preview tags
Status Determination
AUTO-APPROVED = All 4 tests PASS + All 7 Legal requirements PASS

Action: Add to sheet with Status = "AUTO-APPROVED"; ready for production

CONDITIONAL = Any TBD field OR any test/requirement CONDITIONAL

Examples:
- 5 PASS + 2 CONDITIONAL (legal) → Overall CONDITIONAL pending sign-off
- 4 tests PASS + 1+ TBD (ZDR Azure) → CONDITIONAL pending DevOps verification
- Test 2 FAIL (deployment) + threat model submitted → CONDITIONAL pending team review
Action: Add to sheet with Status = "CONDITIONAL"; escalate to responsible team with SLA

BLOCKED = Any test/requirement FAIL without exception OR exception pending security review

Examples:
- Test 4 FAIL (T3 capability) → BLOCKED (escalate to CISO only)
- Test 1 FAIL (PRC) + no exception → BLOCKED
- Test 1 exception approved + threat model pending → CONDITIONAL (not BLOCKED, pending security review)
- Requirement 5 FAIL (PII scope undefined) → BLOCKED
Action: Do NOT add to sheet; escalate with FAIL reason + remediation path


