🛑 EXCEPTION HANDLING
If Test 1 Fails (PRC Origin)
Action: Flag exception; escalate to security team for threat model review
User sees: "Test 1 FAIL: Model vendor is PRC-based. Exception approval required."
User decides: Approve exception (triggers security review) or reject (model BLOCKED)
Next step: Security team receives escalation; conducts threat model assessment; approves or rejects
Result: If security approves → Status = CONDITIONAL; if rejects → Status = BLOCKED
Agent waits: For security team approval before proceeding to sheet update
If Test 2 Fails (Deployment Platform)
Action: Status = CONDITIONAL; flag for requesting team
User/Team action: Requesting team submits deployment threat model + registry + scanning evidence
Escalation: Flag in Jira with SLA (10 business days)
Agent waits: For submission + verification before sheet update
If Test Fails or Legal Requirement Fails (Other)
Action: Flag exception; pause for manual sign-off
User sees: Escalation flag with reason + remediation path
User decides: Approve exception (with justification) or reject
Agent waits: For user approval before proceeding to sheet update
If Data is Missing or Unverifiable
Action: Mark field "TBD" / "PENDING VERIFICATION"
Sheet status: Row posted as "CONDITIONAL" (with TBD fields listed)
Escalation flag: Flag unverified fields in Jira with responsible team + SLA
Example: ZDR Azure/GCP not documented → mark TBD, escalate to DevOps (5-day SLA)
If Model Version Already Exists
Action: Compare version numbers
If higher version: Update existing row (merge logic)
If same version: Report "No changes needed"
If lower version: Report "Trying to add older version; skip"
If Model is Deprecated
Action: Move to "Deprecated" sheet, don't add to main register
Escalation flag: Report deprecation to user
If Multiple Blockers Exist
Action: Stop; report all blockers upfront
User sees: "3 blockers found; cannot proceed"
User decides: Fix issues or abandon model


